              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "dhānya means \"of grain\", and then \"grain, corn\" itself; it is built on dhānā, \"grain\" (CDIAL 6778). It lives on as Hindi dhān, \"growing or unhusked rice\". It is a different word from dhanya, \"fortunate\", in dhanyavādaḥ."
